 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Support (CI Gating)
+The `frai eval` command supports `--threshold <metric>=<min>` to gate CI workflows on metric scores:
+- A threshold passes when a metric's score is at least the minimum (0 to 1).
+- A metric with no score (e.g., exact_match when references are empty) fails its threshold.
+- Exit code: 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 if malformed.
+- The report (JSON and Markdown) includes a `passed` field and `thresholds` list with per-metric outcomes.
+- SDK users: `generateReport` accepts an optional `thresholds` object (`{ exact_match: 0.9 }`); the report structure reflects the same fields as CLI reports.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
